{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"yuyonghao-summarize","displayName":"Summarize","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/yuyonghao-123/skills/yuyonghao-summarize","publisherHandle":"yuyonghao-123","publisherDisplayName":"yuyonghao-123","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/yuyonghao-123","version":"0.1.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1774587633057,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/yuyonghao-summarize/card?ownerHandle=yuyonghao-123&version=0.1.0","sha256":"eb9e15b2735df5e9a0333c0b53172784139faf74eacb27350c106db5d13a6554","size":1930,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"55a5179d64ce0f8a2a913f9f7c640c0b2f3d710d35c773295d7fb54efcb813f9","bundleFingerprints":["1b53f27237f7ac00f028df5a62c4e2a4ab60f9690c7dcefa1937f38087320679","60eb6dec7e1eaff11722d25625f556bfc6e8d04324cae43546294617082fd9fc"],"files":[{"path":"package.json","size":422,"sha256":"1864aa34c4b4be50f91040f28c6e5affeb96e42f7e5ddb09abffed2b47b101a9","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1425,"sha256":"e7cdf499cee3e4ffefdbdca842b4716796cdd983b1f11e1314f295895eeb8161","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":128,"sha256":"90dabb1465a36aae717aa961cbce3d1ccafeb9e44357de466458b160c9a87037","contentType":"application/json"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This summarization skill has a coherent purpose, but users should review it because it installs an unpinned third-party CLI and may send files, URLs, and media to external AI or extraction services.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789437093663,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unverified Third-Party Homebrew Dependency"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":5,"endLine":5}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"ab4b7fe36a476ab0"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `SKILL.md`, line 5  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: `T08: Insecure Dependencies`  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  **Vulnerable Code Snippet**:\n\n  ```yaml\n  metadata: {\"clawdbot\":{\"emoji\":\"🧾\",\"requires\":{\"bins\":[\"summarize\"]},\"install\":[{\"id\":\"brew\",\"kind\":\"brew\",\"formula\":\"steipete/tap/summarize\",\"bins\":[\"summarize\"],\"label\":\"Install summarize (brew)\"}]}}\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The skill directs users or an agent-managed installation process to install the `summarize` executable from the third-party Homebrew tap `steipete/tap`. The formula, executable source, artifact checksum, and immutable version are not included in the audited project. Consequently, the behavior and integrity of the installed component cannot be verified from this package.\n\n  Using a mutable, externally maintained package source creates a supply-chain trust boundary. If the tap, its maintainer account, the referenced release infrastructure, or downloaded artifacts are compromised, installation may deliver code that differs from the code originally reviewed. The project does not pin an immutable formula revision or independently verify an expected artifact digest.\n\n  This finding does not establish that the current third-party formula is malicious. It identifies that the skill delegates executable installation to an unreviewed external source without integrity controls visible in the audited files.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises the third-party Homebrew tap, its maintainer credentials, or an artifact distribution endpoint used by the formula.\n  2. The attacker modifies the formula or a referenced binary/archive to include malicious installation or runtime behavior.\n  3. A user or agent loads the skill and follows its declared installation metadata to obtain the missing `summarize` executable.\n  4. Homebrew resolves and executes the third-party formula and downloads the attacker-controlled component.\n  5. The malicious installation logic or executable runs under the privileges of the account performing the installation.\n  6. The component may access data available to that account whenever the skill invokes `summarize`.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation could execute arbitrary code with the privileges of the user running Homebrew or invoking the installed CLI. The accessible scope could include user-readable files, environment variables, model-provider API keys supplied to the process, network access, and writable user-level configuration or application data.\n\n  The package does not request elevated privileges directly, so administrative or root-level impact is not demonstrated. Such impact would require the installation environment to grant additional privileges independently.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Pin the dependency to an immutable, reviewed release rather than a mutable tap reference.\n  2. Verify downloaded artifacts against a cryptographic SHA-256 or stronger digest maintained in a trusted location.\n  3. Vendor the formula and relevant executable source into a reviewable repository, or use a trusted package registry with provenance and signing support.\n  4. Require signed releases and verify signatures before installation.\n  5. Run installation and execution with least privilege; do not use an administrator account unless strictly necessary.\n  6. Restrict the CLI process to only the files, environment variables, and network destinations required for summarization.\n  7. Add automated dependency provenance checks, checksum validation, and periodic review of the upstream formula and release artifacts.\n  8. Clearly disclose that URLs, local files, and potentially sensitive content may be processed by external model or extraction providers before users invoke the tool."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789437022.6602137,"endTime":1789437057.9351118}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"summarize","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5764znyyvr786pc7ef85km65h8ee5wz-IwRYIK/clawscan-skillspector-821169718/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-15T01:50:20.425988+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":49,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1425,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":6,"executable":false,"size_bytes":128,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package.json","type":"json","lines":19,"executable":false,"size_bytes":422,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d2fc4829e6034181bda193ad356e78bd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":49},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill encourages summarizing URLs, local files, PDFs, images, audio, and YouTube content using third-party model providers and optional extraction services, but it does not clearly warn users that submitted content may be transmitted off-device to external APIs. This creates a real privacy and data-handling risk because users may provide sensitive local files or confidential URLs without understanding that their contents could be sent to OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI, Firecrawl, or Apify.","remediation":"Add an explicit privacy/data-handling warning near the description and quick-start examples stating that URLs, local files, and media content may be sent to third-party services for extraction and summarization. Enumerate which integrations can receive data (LLM providers, Firecrawl, Apify), distinguish local-only behavior from remote processing if applicable, and advise users not to submit secrets, regulated data, or confidential documents without approval.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":49}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1376,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1390},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1493,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1507},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1887,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1901},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1565,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1579},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05"